+<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>deepwiki-architecture-review-2026-10</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=20260922"><script src="search-index.js?v=20260922"></script></head><body><nav><h1><a href="README.html">Sonuvi documentation</a></h1><div class="meta">Canonical source: <code>docs/wiki-source/</code></div><details><summary><strong>Start</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="README.html">README</a></li><li><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a></li><li><a href="using-now-playing.html">Using Sonuvi</a></li><li><a href="core-concepts.html">Core Concepts</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Displays</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="displays.html">Displays</a></li><li><a href="user-interfaces.html">User Interfaces</a></li><li><a href="kiosk-interface.html">Kiosk</a></li><li><a href="visualizer-in-embedded-mode.html">Visualizer</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Playback and Library</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="playback-features.html">Playback Features</a></li><li><a href="queue-and-playback-model.html">Queue and Playback</a></li><li><a href="queue-wizard-internals.html">Queue Wizard</a></li><li><a href="media-library.html">Media Library</a></li><li><a href="listen-on-device.html">Listen on Device</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Integrations</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="integrations.html">Integrations</a></li><li><a href="alexa-interface.html">Alexa</a></li><li><a href="youtube-interface.html">YouTube</a></li><li><a href="radio-interface.html">Radio</a></li><li><a href="mabel-integration.html">Mabel</a></li><li><a href="jukebox-priority-model.html">Jukebox Priority</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Administration</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="configuration-and-administration.html">Configuration and Administration</a></li><li><a href="config-interface.html">Config</a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">Diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">Deployment and Ops</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Developer Reference</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="developer-reference.html">Developer Reference</a></li><li><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a></li><li><a href="api-service-overview.html">API Overview</a></li><li><a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">API Catalog</a></li><li><a href="source-map.html">Source Map</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Troubleshooting and Maintenance</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="troubleshooting-and-technical-notes.html">Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="playback-issue-triage-runbook.html">Playback Triage</a></li><li><a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html">Display Triage</a></li><li><a href="documentation-sources-audit.html">Documentation Audit</a></li><li><a href="wiki-operations.html">Wiki Operations</a></li></ul></details></nav><article><h1 id="sonuvi-server-deepwiki-architectural-review-2026-10">Sonuvi Server — DeepWiki Architectural Review (2026-10)</h1><h2 id="review-status">Review status</h2><ul><li><strong>Review date:</strong> 2026-10-20</li><li><strong>DeepWiki entry point:</strong> <a href="https://deepwiki.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/1-overview">Sonuvi Server overview</a></li><li><strong>DeepWiki publication timestamp shown by the mirror:</strong> 2026-10-20T12:20:14.694701</li><li><strong>DeepWiki source revision:</strong> dee06724c3549b9ab87fc70412ce1043572befab</li><li><strong>Repository revision audited (review baseline):</strong> 8c194c2f2ec2f90fe858b79529d8fbce3460f7b4</li><li><strong>Current branch:</strong> main</li><li><strong>Repository state at review start:</strong> clean; local main and origin/main were identical</li><li><strong>Review artifact:</strong> this report is preserved in canonical <code>docs/wiki-source/</code>; the follow-up code-first reconciliation edits remain uncommitted in an isolated detached worktree until approval</li></ul><p>This is an analysis-first audit. No production code, API contract, service, deployment, iOS repository, or current main worktree was changed.</p><h2 id="executive-assessment">Executive assessment</h2><p>DeepWiki is useful and generally accurate as a compact orientation to the original Sonuvi enhancement layer: moOde/MPD remains a foundational playback domain, the API and static web host form the application tier, the display router is a deliberate stability boundary, and the legacy control surface is protected by a Track Key.</p><p>Its coverage is not a current architectural review of the repository, however. The overview navigation does not expose the complete numbered hierarchy. A recursive traversal of every same-repository DeepWiki link found and fetched 79 URL variants; after normalizing duplicate aliases and two non-page trailing artifacts, it covered <strong>77 canonical numbered pages across sections 1–11</strong>. Every canonical page reported the same publication timestamp and source revision recorded above. No same-repository DeepWiki page linked by the traversed hierarchy was left unvisited.</p><p>The complete page inventory was:</p><ul><li><strong>1 — Overview:</strong> Overview; System Architecture; Installation and Setup;</li></ul><p>Key Concepts.</p><ul><li><strong>2 — User Interfaces:</strong> User Interfaces; Application Shell; Now Playing</li></ul><p>Displays; Mobile Controller Dashboard; Kiosk Mode; Diagnostics Interface; Tablet Controller; Library Browse Panes; Desktop Display; Mobile Display.</p><ul><li><strong>3 — Display Enhancement System:</strong> Display Enhancement System; Overview</li></ul><p>and Push Model; Peppy Builder and Renderer; Player Builder and Renderer; Display Router; Audio Data Pipeline; Peppy Skin Assets and Export.</p><ul><li><strong>4 — Queue Management:</strong> Queue Management; Queue Wizard Interface; Filter</li></ul><p>Builder; Vibe Discovery; Playlist and Podcast Queues; Live Queue Editing.</p><ul><li><strong>5 — Media Library:</strong> Media Library; Library Health Dashboard; Static Album</li></ul><p>Art; Animated Art System; Metadata Inspector; Podcast Management; Radio Station Browser.</p><ul><li><strong>6 — Playback Features:</strong> Playback Features; Now Playing System; Transport</li></ul><p>Controls; Ratings and Favorites; Progress and State Tracking; Listen on Device; Listening History and Scrobbling.</p><ul><li><strong>7 — External Integrations:</strong> External Integrations; Alexa Voice Control;</li></ul><p>moOde Integration; Last.fm Vibe Discovery; YouTube Proxy; iTunes and Motion Art APIs; Seeburg and Multiphone Jukebox Integrations; Mills Throne Jukebox Integration; Echo Link Volume Bridge; UPnP Control Point and Qobuz Connect.</p><ul><li><strong>8 — Theme &amp; Customization:</strong> Theme &amp; Customization; Theme Token System;</li></ul><p>Theme Editor; Responsive Layouts; Peppy Skins and Customization.</p><ul><li><strong>9 — Backend API:</strong> Backend API; API Architecture; Core Endpoints; MPD</li></ul><p>Integration; SSH Bridge; Cache Systems; Mobile and CarPlay API; Audio Info and Source Diagnostics.</p><ul><li><strong>10 — Configuration &amp; Administration:</strong> Configuration &amp; Administration;</li></ul><p>Configuration Interface; Runtime Verification; Service Control; Diagnostics Tools; moOde Overrides and Ops Units.</p><ul><li><strong>11 — Development:</strong> Development; Development Setup; API Extension; UI</li></ul><p>Component Patterns; Testing and Debugging; Documentation Pipeline; Public Sonuvi Site and CI.</p><p>The relevant <a href="https://deepwiki.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/7.9-upnp-control-point-and-qobuz-connect">UPnP Control Point &amp; Qobuz Connect</a> page therefore is part of the full audit, not an isolated exception. The traversal also checked each page&#x27;s same-repository navigation links; external source/documentation references were treated as evidence to compare against the current checkout rather than as additional DeepWiki pages.</p><p>The reviewed pages point at dee06724. Current main contains a later, material change set: 15 files differ from that revision, with 986 insertions and 72 deletions. The delta includes the Qobuz Connect control/release lifecycle, mobile routes, current UPnP session handling, and the associated tests and documentation. Page 7.9 provides meaningful coverage of UPnP, mobile UPnP, Qobuz observation, identity boundaries, tests, and the iOS handoff, but it still describes the older read-only Qobuz control boundary. The initial claim that only four pages existed was incorrect; the complete 77-page inventory above is the basis for the findings below.</p><p><strong>Overall classification: PARTIALLY CORRECT, materially incomplete for the current Server.</strong> DeepWiki is safe as a legacy-topology starting point. It must not be treated as the current source of truth for playback authority, queue ownership, authentication, Qobuz, UPnP, mobile contracts, or iOS architecture.</p><p>Direct requests to DeepWiki returned a Vercel HTTP 429 challenge during this audit. The pages were reviewed through the read-only Jina mirror, which returned page text, links, source references, and revision identifiers. The mirror did not expose a complete tree from the overview alone, so the audit followed section-parent links recursively and verified the resulting full same-repository inventory rather than treating the overview navigation as complete.</p><h2 id="1-comparison-baseline">1. Comparison baseline</h2><h3 id="repository-state">Repository state</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Branch</td><td>main</td></tr><tr><td>Local HEAD</td><td>8c194c2 — fix(upnp): wait for renderer readiness before play</td></tr><tr><td>origin/main</td><td>8c194c2</td></tr><tr><td>Ahead/behind</td><td>0 / 0</td></tr><tr><td>Worktree</td><td>Clean</td></tr><tr><td>DeepWiki revision</td><td>dee06724 — Revise README for improved clarity and details</td></tr><tr><td>Current-vs-DeepWiki delta</td><td>15 files; 986 insertions, 72 deletions</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The current revision includes, among other changes:</p><ul><li>Qobuz Connect control and release code</li><li>the PiBuZ Qobuz control adapter</li><li>mobile Qobuz, UPnP, local-source, playback-event, and history routes</li><li>current UPnP renderer-session/readiness logic</li><li>audio and route-contract tests</li><li>current Qobuz and UPnP documentation updates</li></ul><p>The review did not clean, reset, stash, rebase, merge, deploy, restart, or commit anything in the active repository.</p><h3 id="authority-order-used-for-the-comparison">Authority order used for the comparison</h3><p>The comparison followed the repository&#x27;s documented precedence:</p><ol><li>Current source code and verified repository contracts</li><li>Canonical editable documentation in docs/wiki-source/</li><li>Root documentation and runbooks</li><li>DeepWiki&#x27;s derived pages</li></ol><p>DeepWiki was used as an independent architectural description, not as an authority.</p><h2 id="2-coverage-comparison">2. Coverage comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Area requested for review</th><th>DeepWiki coverage</th><th>Current assessment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>System overview and legacy topology</td><td>Strong</td><td>Mostly VERIFIED</td></tr><tr><td>Backend services and routing</td><td>High-level only</td><td>PARTIALLY CORRECT; current route families are much broader</td></tr><tr><td>moOde/MPD integration</td><td>Strong</td><td>VERIFIED for the MPD domain; incomplete as a whole-system model</td></tr><tr><td>Playback authority and state</td><td>Legacy MPD-centered view</td><td>PARTIALLY CORRECT and potentially misleading without source qualification</td></tr><tr><td>Queue management and Queue Wizard</td><td>Not meaningfully covered</td><td>Incomplete</td></tr><tr><td>Vibe Radio and Last.fm</td><td>Not meaningfully covered</td><td>Incomplete</td></tr><tr><td>Listening history and scrobbling</td><td>Page 6.6 is titled for this topic, but its body explicitly says the supplied material does not establish history/scrobbling and instead documents About/Apple enrichment</td><td>DeepWiki coverage is mislabeled and does not establish the current shared event pipeline</td></tr><tr><td>Library and metadata</td><td>Substantial pieces across sections 5, 6.6, and 7.5</td><td>Useful orientation, but the current provider-neutral About/Apple contract and ownership are clearer in canonical docs</td></tr><tr><td>Display, Peppy, Player, visualizer, kiosk</td><td>Good legacy coverage</td><td>Mostly VERIFIED; operational details need current deployment links</td></tr><tr><td>Classic/controller/tablet/mobile interfaces</td><td>Partial; page 7.9 covers mobile UPnP and handoff boundaries</td><td>Current bearer contract is broader than the reviewed DeepWiki material</td></tr><tr><td>UPnP control point and renderer</td><td>Substantial coverage on page 7.9</td><td>Useful and mostly aligned, but current readiness/control details need re-checking</td></tr><tr><td>Qobuz Connect</td><td>Substantial observation/integration coverage on page 7.9</td><td>Observation is useful; control/release behavior is outdated at dee06724</td></tr><tr><td>Audio Info and source diagnostics</td><td>Substantial coverage in page 9.7</td><td>Foundation is source-backed; current mobile wrapper, freshness, and revision-specific fields still need reconciliation</td></tr><tr><td>Alexa and external integrations</td><td>Partial Alexa mention</td><td>Incomplete; Seeburg, Multiphone/Mabel, Mills, Echo Link, and current boundaries are absent</td></tr><tr><td>Deployment, configuration, and services</td><td>Installer-oriented</td><td>PARTIALLY CORRECT; live Pi5 deployment and recovery model are absent</td></tr><tr><td>Testing and troubleshooting</td><td>Minimal</td><td>Incomplete</td></tr><tr><td>Native iOS boundary</td><td>Partial page-7.9 handoff coverage</td><td>Standalone device-owned catalog direction remains incomplete</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="3-deepwiki-claim-classification">3. DeepWiki claim classification</h2><h3 id="verified-claims">VERIFIED claims</h3><p>The following claims are supported by the current source and documentation, with the scope qualifications noted below:</p><ol><li>**The application has a moOde/MPD foundation, an app-host API/web tier,</li></ol><p>and browser/display surfaces.** The current root <a href="architecture.html">architecture.md</a> and <a href="architecture.html">architecture.md</a> describe this same split.</p><ol><li><strong>The API and static web service are normally separate listeners.</strong> The</li></ol><p>documented defaults remain API port 3101 and static UI port 8101. The stable display router is intentionally served from the UI surface rather than being tied to a fragile display implementation.</p><ol><li><strong>The public state routes are central integration surfaces.</strong> The</li></ol><p>/now-playing and /next-up family remains important to displays, controllers, and integrations, although current source-specific state is richer than the DeepWiki description implies.</p><ol><li>**Track Key protection remains real for the classic/server control</li></ol><p>surface.** DeepWiki correctly identifies a bearer-like Track Key boundary for legacy control and configuration routes. This is not the only authentication domain in the current system.</p><ol><li>**moOde/MPD integration uses the host&#x27;s existing player state and tools</li></ol><p>rather than replacing moOde.** The current implementation still uses MPD and moOde-specific integration paths for MPD playback, queue, metadata, and hardware-facing behavior.</p><ol><li><strong>The display layer has explicit modes and a builder-first Peppy path.</strong></li></ol><p>The current display and Peppy documentation supports the DeepWiki description of a stable display entry point, mode selection, and generated renderer state.</p><ol><li>**The UI commonly observes normalized server state rather than directly</li></ol><p>coupling every surface to MPD.** This remains a useful design principle, but the normalized state now also has Qobuz, UPnP, radio, AirPlay, and device/mobile qualifications.</p><h3 id="partially-correct-claims">PARTIALLY CORRECT claims</h3><ol><li><strong>“MPD is the audio authority.”</strong></li></ol><p>This is correct for the MPD playback domain. It is not a universal authority statement for the Server. Current playback authority is source- and target-dependent:</p><p>- MPD/moOde owns the Home/local/radio paths that use MPD. - Qobuz Connect is observed and controlled through the enhanced PiBuZ receiver, with a separate remote queue and playback state. - UPnP has a Sonuvi control-point/renderer session and logical queue boundary; it is not just an MPD stream label. - native iOS playback has device-local state and uses Server contracts for shared observation/history during the transition.</p><p>The current <a href="playback-authority-by-mode.html">playback-authority-by-mode.md</a> already has the right direction but needs Qobuz and current UPnP sections.</p><ol><li><strong>“The API is a stable router over moOde/library state.”</strong></li></ol><p>The API is still a stable control-plane boundary, but it now owns or mediates more than moOde/library state: mobile bearer sessions, Qobuz/PiBuZ observation and control, UPnP discovery and renderer sessions, audio diagnostics, history events, metadata enrichment, and external hardware integrations.</p><ol><li><strong>“Track Key is the primary authorization model.”</strong></li></ol><p>Track Key remains primary for the classic web/controller routes. Native mobile routes use signed bearer sessions and scoped media/radio tickets. Mobile routes must not be described as raw Track-Key or raw MPD access. The current <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/src/lib/mobile-auth.mjs">mobile-auth.mjs</a> and <a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">api-endpoint-catalog.md</a> establish the split.</p><ol><li><strong>“UPnP is a stream-like playback mode.”</strong></li></ol><p>That shorthand appears in the older overview material, while DeepWiki page 7.9 provides a much more accurate control-point, renderer-session, mobile-bridge, and logical-queue description. The 7.9 treatment is a valuable architectural insight. Current main still extends it with the newer readiness polling, stale-observation protection, and duplicate-Play handling, so the page remains revision-stale rather than being absent or fundamentally wrong.</p><ol><li>**“Installation is represented by the installer and systemd/PM2</li></ol><p>configuration described by DeepWiki.”**</p><p>The installer concepts are still useful. The live operational model also includes the Pi5 deployment helper, the installed systemd service, path-specific restart behavior, host-key pinning, and post-deployment verification. DeepWiki&#x27;s excerpt did not establish the actual unit contents or the current Pi5 recovery procedure.</p><ol><li><strong>“The API and web host are the main application boundary.”</strong></li></ol><p>This remains true, but source-specific remote systems and native mobile clients introduce explicit ownership boundaries inside that application boundary. A single “Server controls the player” statement is too broad.</p><h3 id="outdated-descriptions-or-implications">OUTDATED descriptions or implications</h3><ol><li><strong>The analyzed revision is outdated.</strong> DeepWiki&#x27;s source references stop at</li></ol><p>dee06724. Current main adds the Qobuz, mobile, and current UPnP changes listed in the baseline.</p><ol><li><strong>The implied UPnP capability is outdated.</strong> Current UPnP is a guarded</li></ol><p>control-point and renderer-session subsystem, not merely a stream-like display mode.</p><ol><li><strong>The apparent completeness of the route inventory is outdated.</strong> Pages</li></ol><p>9.2, 9.6, and 9.7 cover important API and diagnostics families, but they predate the current main route set. Current Server additions include the expanded Qobuz controls/release lifecycle, mobile UPnP mutations, local-source, playback-event, history, and revision-specific audio-info behavior.</p><ol><li><strong>The deployment description is operationally incomplete.</strong> It does not</li></ol><p>describe the current primary Pi5 deployment helper, live service restart rules, or the verification requirements used for current backend changes.</p><ol><li><strong>The documentation corpus itself has moved.</strong> The repository&#x27;s canonical</li></ol><p>editable knowledge base is docs/wiki-source/, with focused source-backed pages and runbooks. DeepWiki should not be treated as a second maintained documentation hierarchy.</p><h3 id="incorrect-when-interpreted-as-a-current-complete-architecture">INCORRECT when interpreted as a current complete architecture</h3><p>No isolated sentence in the reviewed DeepWiki pages was proven flatly false against current source when read as a description of the original moOde-centered foundation. The following interpretation would be incorrect:</p><blockquote>Sonuvi Server is only an MPD/moOde enhancement layer with one queue, one control authority, one Track-Key authorization model, and no independent Qobuz, UPnP, mobile, or native-device ownership boundaries.</blockquote><p>That is not the current architecture. The safer classification for individual DeepWiki statements is PARTIALLY CORRECT, with the completeness implication classified as INCORRECT.</p><h3 id="unverified-claims">UNVERIFIED claims</h3><p>The following could not be established from the available DeepWiki material and were not asserted as current facts:</p><ul><li>exact contents, ordering, dependencies, and failure behavior of every</li></ul><p>systemd unit</p><ul><li>exact PM2 ecosystem behavior in the current deployment</li><li>whether every installer option still matches the live Pi5 installation</li><li>current runtime behavior of the live service, because this audit did not</li></ul><p>restart services, deploy, or perform live playback tests</p><ul><li>current Qobuz account/library behavior beyond the repository contracts</li><li>runtime behavior of external hardware that is separately maintained</li></ul><p>These require source inspection, deployment inspection, or a deliberately authorized runtime test; they should not be inferred from DeepWiki.</p><h2 id="4-current-architectural-relationships-deepwiki-does-not-fully-capture">4. Current architectural relationships DeepWiki does not fully capture</h2><h3 id="41-multiple-playback-authorities-and-targets">4.1 Multiple playback authorities and targets</h3><p>The current system is better represented as a set of source/target domains than as a single player:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>State/control owner</th><th>Queue or identity boundary</th><th>Server role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home/local/radio through moOde</td><td>moOde/MPD</td><td>MPD queue and MPD/file-derived identity</td><td>Control, normalization, queue shaping, history observation</td></tr><tr><td>Qobuz Connect</td><td>Enhanced PiBuZ receiver for remote playback</td><td>Remote Qobuz queue/occurrence and PiBuZ observation</td><td>Observe, expose status/queue, issue guarded controls, perform explicit handoff/release</td></tr><tr><td>UPnP/OpenHome renderer</td><td>Sonuvi UPnP control point plus selected renderer</td><td>Process/session-owned logical queue and renderer transport</td><td>Discover, select, preflight, control, serialize startup, expose sanitized state</td></tr><tr><td>Native iOS playback</td><td>iOS device</td><td>Device-owned native queue/cache/catalog direction</td><td>Current contracts, metadata/identity bridge, playback-event/history ingestion</td></tr><tr><td>AirPlay and other external paths</td><td>External receiver/target</td><td>Source-specific external transport</td><td>Observe and normalize where supported; do not assume MPD ownership</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The important distinction is between <strong>who currently plays bytes</strong>, <strong>who owns the queue</strong>, <strong>who owns identity</strong>, and <strong>who reports shared history</strong>. Those are not always the same component.</p><h3 id="42-multiple-queues">4.2 Multiple queues</h3><p>The current documentation distinguishes playback from queue shaping, but it needs a single cross-system matrix. At minimum, the Server now has:</p><ul><li>the moOde/MPD live queue</li><li>the Qobuz remote queue, including occurrence-preserving jump/control</li><li>the UPnP logical queue and renderer session</li><li>native iOS Home/device queues</li><li>saved Qobuz queues, which are durable remote captures rather than the live</li></ul><p>MPD queue</p><p>Queue position, upcoming items, duplicates, persistence, and control commands therefore require source-specific semantics. A generic “Next Up is the queue” explanation is unsafe.</p><h3 id="43-multiple-authentication-domains">4.3 Multiple authentication domains</h3><p>The current authorization boundaries are not interchangeable:</p><ul><li>Track Key for classic/server control and configuration</li><li>signed mobile bearer sessions with scopes and expiry</li><li>short-lived mobile media/radio tickets where required</li><li>provider/receiver credentials and internal PiBuZ access</li><li>network and renderer trust boundaries for UPnP</li></ul><p>The mobile boundary deliberately avoids exposing raw Track Keys, MPD paths, filesystem paths, or provider credentials to the native app.</p><h3 id="44-multiple-identity-systems">4.4 Multiple identity systems</h3><p>Track Keys, MPD file identity, Qobuz/PiBuZ identifiers, UPnP object/resource references, and mobile opaque IDs are not interchangeable. The history pipeline must qualify and deduplicate at the appropriate boundary instead of assuming that a displayed title or artwork URL is a canonical identity.</p><h3 id="45-shared-history-and-scrobbling">4.5 Shared history and scrobbling</h3><p>The current history design is a server-side event pipeline:</p><ol><li>source-specific observation or an explicit mobile playback event enters the</li></ol><p>Server</p><ol><li>the Server resolves/validates identity and source attribution</li><li>qualification and deduplication are applied</li><li>local history is recorded</li><li>Last.fm submission is performed asynchronously when eligible</li></ol><p>The MPD poller remains important, but it is not the only possible event source. Qobuz and Sonuvi-owned UPnP playback require suppression or qualification rules so that MPD observations do not create duplicate history. Native iOS reports through POST /v1/mobile/playback/events; it does not submit directly to Last.fm.</p><p>The existing <a href="centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.html">centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.md</a> documents most of this well, but its current-mode wording and review date need reconciliation.</p><h3 id="46-audio-diagnostics-distinguish-facts-from-configuration">4.6 Audio diagnostics distinguish facts from configuration</h3><p>The current Audio Info contract separates:</p><ul><li>source-reported format</li><li>decoded PCM</li><li>configured output</li><li>hardware-measured output</li><li>processing and volume configuration</li><li>conversion uncertainty</li><li>freshness and diagnostic provenance</li></ul><p>Configured moOde output is not proof of measured DAC output. A stopped MPD stream is not proof that a Qobuz or external stream has no open hardware path. DeepWiki page 9.7 covers the underlying moOde, ALSA, and source-probe distinction, while the current <a href="diagnostics-interface.html">diagnostics-interface.md</a> and mobile contract add the repository-specific sanitization, freshness, and measured/configured semantics that still require reconciliation.</p><h3 id="47-metadata-enrichment-is-provider-neutral">4.7 Metadata enrichment is provider-neutral</h3><p>The current About architecture presents provider-neutral metadata to clients, with optional Apple Music editorial enrichment and bounded caching. Playback must not depend on an About lookup. DeepWiki covers portions of this through the Media Library, Metadata Inspector, iTunes/Motion Art, and page-6.6 About material, but page 6.6 is mislabeled as listening history and the current provider-neutral contract is clearer in <a href="about-metadata.html">about-metadata.md</a> and <a href="apple-about-metadata.html">apple-about-metadata.md</a>.</p><h2 id="5-newer-subsystem-findings">5. Newer subsystem findings</h2><h3 id="qobuz-connect">Qobuz Connect</h3><p>Current source and documentation establish a working Server/PiBuZ bridge with separate observation and guarded control responsibilities:</p><ul><li>the mobile API exposes Qobuz snapshot, queue, saved-queue, artwork, and</li></ul><p>playback-control routes</p><ul><li>supported controls include play, resume, pause, next, previous, seek, and</li></ul><p>queue occurrence jump</p><ul><li>the control adapter performs freshness/expectation checks and read-after-</li></ul><p>write verification where possible</p><ul><li>explicit renderer release/handoff is a separate lifecycle operation</li><li>Qobuz playback is not the same thing as browsing an authenticated Qobuz</li></ul><p>library in the Sonuvi catalog</p><ul><li>Qobuz queue occurrences and duplicates must be preserved</li></ul><p>Relevant source includes <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/src/lib/pibuz-qobuz-control.mjs">pibuz-qobuz-control.mjs</a>, <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/src/lib/qobuz-connect-control.mjs">qobuz-connect-control.mjs</a>, <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/src/lib/qobuz-connect-release.mjs">qobuz-connect-release.mjs</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/src/routes/mobile.routes.mjs">mobile.routes.mjs</a>.</p><p>The existing <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/docs/runbooks/28-qobuz-connect-now-playing.md"><code>docs/runbooks/28-qobuz-connect-now-playing.md</code></a> contains useful provenance and release material, but parts of its Phase 1 description are now stale: it still describes the adapter as read-only and the earlier worktree as intentionally undeployed, while current main exposes the control routes and the tested release lifecycle. The historical Phase 1 language should be separated from the current implementation before that runbook is used as an agent instruction.</p><p>The Qobuz media-server experiment in <a href="https://github.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/blob/main/docs/runbooks/29-upnp-queue-and-qobuz-media-server-poc.md"><code>docs/runbooks/29-upnp-queue-and-qobuz-media-server-poc.md</code></a> must remain clearly separate from the working PiBuZ/Qobuz Connect path.</p><h3 id="upnp-and-renderer-control">UPnP and renderer control</h3><p>The current UPnP architecture includes:</p><ul><li>discovery and renderer selection</li><li>browse/search and resource selection</li><li>renderer capability and transport inspection</li><li>preflight and session ownership</li><li>readiness polling before Play</li><li>stale-observation protection</li><li>duplicate-Play prevention after ambiguous SOAP responses</li><li>logical queue and occurrence control</li><li>mobile sanitization and authorization</li></ul><p>The recent current-main change specifically waits for the expected renderer URI and readiness conditions before issuing Play, with a bounded fallback. DeepWiki page 7.9 captures the main control-point and queue protocol. Current main extends that description with the newer failure-sensitive readiness, stale-observation, and duplicate-Play behavior.</p><p>The current <a href="upnp-control-point.html">upnp-control-point.md</a> is the right canonical home, but should cross-link the current session/readiness behavior and explicitly state which state belongs to the renderer, the Sonuvi control point, or MPD.</p><h3 id="audio-diagnostics">Audio diagnostics</h3><p>The current GET /v1/mobile/audio-info contract is a sanitized mobile wrapper around the Track-Key-protected moOde/audio diagnostics path. It returns versioned, structured information and distinguishes measured values from configured values and unknown conversion. The mobile response does not expose filesystem paths, raw diagnostic commands, or private connection details.</p><p>DeepWiki page 9.7 covers the foundation of this behavior: the protected moOde/audio-info path, optional ALSA measurement, local source probing, and sanitized mobile diagnostics. It does not establish the current main revision&#x27;s complete mobile wrapper, freshness fields, Qobuz/source handling, or exact privacy-redaction contract. This is therefore a reconciliation gap, not an absence of DeepWiki coverage.</p><h3 id="listening-history">Listening history</h3><p>The current history implementation is broader than MPD polling:</p><ul><li>source attribution is explicit</li><li>canonical/opaque identity resolution is validated</li><li>qualification and deduplication are server-owned</li><li>MPD observations remain a production input</li><li>mobile native playback reports progress/history through the mobile event</li></ul><p>route</p><ul><li>source-specific suppression prevents duplicate Qobuz/UPnP observations</li><li>Last.fm submission is asynchronous and does not define local history</li></ul><p>The DeepWiki page titled <a href="https://deepwiki.com/teacherguy2020/now-playing/6.6-listening-history-and-scrobbling">Listening History and Scrobbling</a> is a material documentation-generation defect: its own text says the supplied files do not establish local history or Last.fm behavior, while the sources it actually discusses are <code>about-card.js</code>, <code>about.service.mjs</code>, and <code>apple-about.service.mjs</code>. Page 7.9 does not fill that gap. The current history/scrobbling pipeline therefore remains absent from the reviewed DeepWiki content, and the mislabeled 6.6 page must not be treated as evidence for it.</p><h3 id="external-hardware-and-integrations">External hardware and integrations</h3><p>The current API registers and/or mediates several separately owned systems, including Seeburg, Multiphone/Mabel, Mills, Echo Link, moOde, AirPlay, UPnP, Qobuz/PiBuZ, Alexa, radio, podcasts, and YouTube. The Server is not the implementation owner of every external system. The integration boundary should identify for each system:</p><ul><li>device/service owner</li><li>Server responsibility</li><li>direction of control and observation</li><li>credentials and trust boundary</li><li>history/scrobble attribution</li><li>failure/recovery behavior</li></ul><p>DeepWiki&#x27;s Alexa and moOde coverage is not enough to establish that matrix.</p><h2 id="6-canonical-documentation-comparison">6. Canonical documentation comparison</h2><h3 id="strong-existing-material">Strong existing material</h3><p>The following pages are more current or more nuanced than the corresponding DeepWiki coverage:</p><ul><li><a href="architecture.html">architecture.md</a> — explains the API control plane,</li></ul><p>display renderer, queue/playback mediation, and integration boundaries</p><ul><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">deployment-and-ops.md</a> — explains app-host,</li></ul><p>moOde-host, and host-override responsibilities and restart verification</p><ul><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">diagnostics-interface.md</a> — documents measured</li></ul><p>versus configured audio information</p><ul><li><a href="mobile-now-playing.html">mobile-now-playing.md</a> — documents the mobile</li></ul><p>bearer boundary, local-source manifest, playback events, and sanitized state</p><ul><li><a href="mobile-live-queue.html">mobile-live-queue.md</a> — documents target-owned</li></ul><p>queues and current Qobuz/mobile queue semantics</p><ul><li><a href="centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.html">centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.md</a></li></ul><p>— documents shared history and Last.fm qualification</p><ul><li><a href="about-metadata.html">about-metadata.md</a> and</li></ul><p><a href="apple-about-metadata.html">apple-about-metadata.md</a> — document provider- neutral About enrichment and optional Apple credentials</p><ul><li><a href="deepwiki-structure-mapping.html">deepwiki-structure-mapping.md</a> — already</li></ul><p>establishes that DeepWiki-style organization should inform, not replace, the canonical wiki</p><h3 id="gaps-and-contradictions">Gaps and contradictions</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Existing page</th><th>Finding</th><th>Recommended treatment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>architecture.md</td><td>Strong conceptual model, but its integration summary is mostly pre-Qobuz/mobile/modern-UPnP</td><td>Add a current source/authority matrix and link to existing focused pages</td></tr><tr><td>system-overview.md</td><td>Broad overview omits Qobuz, UPnP control point, native iOS, and external hardware ownership</td><td>Add a concise current-system map, not a second hierarchy</td></tr><tr><td>api-service-overview.md</td><td>Describes Track Key as the main request distinction and does not fully explain bearer/mobile scope</td><td>Add authentication domains and route-family ownership</td></tr><tr><td>api-endpoint-catalog.md</td><td>Has a useful mobile section, but current Qobuz Connect and mobile UPnP routes are not fully cataloged</td><td>Add current route families, auth, mutation, and source-ownership notes</td></tr><tr><td>playback-authority-by-mode.md</td><td>Correctly says authority is mode-dependent, but lacks Qobuz Connect and modern UPnP ownership</td><td>Add source/target/control/state distinctions</td></tr><tr><td>queue-and-playback-model.md</td><td>Separates queue from playback but lacks a cross-system queue matrix</td><td>Add MPD, Qobuz, UPnP, saved-queue, and native-device semantics</td></tr><tr><td>integrations.md</td><td>Omits Qobuz/PiBuZ, UPnP, Echo Link, native iOS, and current mobile contracts</td><td>Make this the integration ownership index</td></tr><tr><td>centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.md</td><td>Strong content, but current mode wording/review date need reconciliation</td><td>Update current MPD/Qobuz/UPnP behavior and resolve shadow/active wording</td></tr><tr><td>diagnostics-interface.md</td><td>Strong Audio Info semantics</td><td>Cross-link from API and mobile pages; keep measured/configured distinctions prominent</td></tr><tr><td>mobile-now-playing.md</td><td>Strong current mobile boundary</td><td>Cross-link Qobuz/UPnP route families and explicitly label transition versus target architecture</td></tr><tr><td>runbooks/28-qobuz-connect-now-playing.md</td><td>Contains stale read-only and undeployed Phase 1 statements</td><td>Correct historical/current separation before relying on it</td></tr><tr><td>runbooks/29-upnp-queue-and-qobuz-media-server-poc.md</td><td>Historical PoC language and old test/deployment notes can be confused with working Qobuz Connect</td><td>Mark status and boundaries clearly</td></tr><tr><td>deployment-and-ops.md</td><td>More operationally accurate than DeepWiki, but should mention the current Pi5 helper and file-scoped restart rule</td><td>Add a short current deployment reference</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The existing structure is sufficient. This audit does not recommend creating a parallel DeepWiki-derived hierarchy.</p><h2 id="7-documentation-improvement-plan">7. Documentation improvement plan</h2><p>Prioritized work should remain within docs/wiki-source/ and existing runbook families:</p><h3 id="priority-0-correct-agent-facing-contradictions">Priority 0 — correct agent-facing contradictions</h3><ol><li>Update runbooks/28-qobuz-connect-now-playing.md to distinguish the</li></ol><p>historical read-only Phase 1 adapter from the current guarded playback controls and release/restart lifecycle.</p><ol><li>Mark the Qobuz media-server PoC in runbooks/29 as separate from the working</li></ol><p>PiBuZ bridge and refresh historical test/deployment statements.</p><ol><li>Add a warning to playback-authority-by-mode.md that MPD authority is</li></ol><p>domain-specific, not universal.</p><h3 id="priority-1-add-one-coherent-current-architecture-map">Priority 1 — add one coherent current architecture map</h3><ol><li>Extend architecture.md with a compact matrix for:</li></ol><p>- playback/source authority - queue owner - identity owner - authentication boundary - history event path</p><ol><li>Extend integrations.md as the ownership index for moOde, Qobuz/PiBuZ,</li></ol><p>UPnP, native iOS, Alexa, Seeburg, Multiphone/Mabel, Mills, Echo Link, radio, podcasts, YouTube, and Last.fm.</p><ol><li>Extend api-service-overview.md and api-endpoint-catalog.md with current</li></ol><p>mobile bearer, Qobuz, UPnP, Audio Info, local-source, playback-event, and history route families.</p><ol><li>Extend queue-and-playback-model.md with the multiple-queue matrix.</li></ol><h3 id="priority-2-reconcile-focused-contracts">Priority 2 — reconcile focused contracts</h3><ol><li>Refresh centralized-playback-history-and-scrobbling.md with current</li></ol><p>Qobuz/UPnP suppression and MPD mode wording.</p><ol><li>Cross-link diagnostics-interface.md, mobile-now-playing.md, and the</li></ol><p>current source implementation so measured/configured/unknown fields remain consistent.</p><ol><li>Cross-link upnp-control-point.md to current readiness, stale-session, and</li></ol><p>duplicate-Play behavior.</p><ol><li>Add current deployment-helper and service-verification notes to</li></ol><p>deployment-and-ops.md.</p><h3 id="what-not-to-do">What not to do</h3><ul><li>Do not copy DeepWiki pages into docs/wiki-source/.</li><li>Do not create a second DeepWiki-shaped navigation tree.</li><li>Do not describe planned native catalog ownership as implemented.</li><li>Do not collapse MPD, Qobuz, UPnP, and native iOS queues into one generic</li></ul><p>queue contract.</p><ul><li>Do not expose raw Track Keys, MPD paths, filesystem paths, or provider</li></ul><p>credentials in mobile documentation.</p><h2 id="8-serverios-architectural-boundary">8. Server/iOS architectural boundary</h2><p>DeepWiki page 7.9 covers part of the UPnP/Qobuz handoff boundary, but it does not settle the current standalone native iOS transition or the approved device-owned catalog target.</p><h3 id="current-server-responsibilities">Current Server responsibilities</h3><p>During the transition, the Server currently provides or mediates:</p><ul><li>existing opaque mobile track identities and metadata resolution</li><li>Home queue/playback contracts</li><li>current mobile now-playing, next-up, Audio Info, and queue contracts</li><li>Qobuz Connect observation/control contracts</li><li>UPnP discovery/control contracts</li><li>local-source manifest availability</li><li>native playback-event ingestion for shared history</li><li>server-side qualification, deduplication, and Last.fm submission</li></ul><h3 id="current-native-client-responsibilities">Current native-client responsibilities</h3><p>The native client owns its device UI, local playback mechanisms, and local storage/cache behavior. It uses scoped Server contracts for shared state, identity resolution, local-source availability, and history observation rather than receiving raw server internals.</p><h3 id="target-architecture-not-yet-implemented">Target architecture not yet implemented</h3><p>The approved direction is an iOS-device-owned canonical Sonuvi Catalog with provider aggregation, persistent recording identity, attached-SSD observations/cache, and server-independent native playback. The target catalog authority, provider aggregation, canonical enrichment, and server-independent playback are not implemented in the current Server.</p><p>Documentation and future changes must label these as target behavior. They must not silently replace current opaque MobileTrack, Home queue, or mobile contract semantics.</p><h3 id="shared-contracts-that-matter-now">Shared contracts that matter now</h3><ul><li>GET /v1/mobile/local-source/manifest</li><li>POST /v1/mobile/playback/events</li><li>GET /v1/mobile/audio-info</li><li>current mobile now-playing/next-up and queue contracts</li><li>Qobuz Connect and mobile UPnP contracts where the native client uses them</li></ul><p>The iOS client should remain on these explicit contracts. It should not reimplement Server-side playback arbitration or infer identity from artwork, titles, raw paths, or provider-specific URLs.</p><h2 id="9-risks-revealed-by-the-comparison">9. Risks revealed by the comparison</h2><ol><li><strong>Authority confusion:</strong> an MPD-only explanation can cause a future agent</li></ol><p>to mutate MPD while Qobuz or UPnP owns playback.</p><ol><li><strong>Queue confusion:</strong> treating Next Up, the MPD queue, a remote Qobuz queue,</li></ol><p>and a UPnP logical queue as interchangeable can lose occurrence identity or issue controls to the wrong target.</p><ol><li><strong>Authentication confusion:</strong> treating mobile bearer sessions as Track</li></ol><p>Keys can produce contract or security errors.</p><ol><li><strong>Documentation drift:</strong> stale Qobuz runbook statements currently conflict</li></ol><p>with current control code and can lead to an unnecessary read-only design.</p><ol><li><strong>History duplication:</strong> external-source and MPD observations must retain</li></ol><p>explicit suppression/qualification rules.</p><ol><li><strong>Diagnostics overclaiming:</strong> configured output must not be reported as</li></ol><p>measured hardware output.</p><ol><li><strong>iOS future-state leakage:</strong> target device-owned catalog behavior must not</li></ol><p>be presented as current implementation.</p><ol><li><strong>DeepWiki revision skew:</strong> a derived page can appear comprehensive while</li></ol><p>predating a large feature set; the analyzed revision must always be recorded beside conclusions.</p><ol><li><strong>Operational mismatch:</strong> installer documentation alone does not prove the</li></ol><p>live service lifecycle, deployment helper, restart behavior, or recovery state.</p><h2 id="10-highest-priority-recommendations">10. Highest-priority recommendations</h2><ol><li>Treat DeepWiki as a useful legacy orientation and independent terminology</li></ol><p>review, not as an architectural source of truth.</p><ol><li>Correct the stale Qobuz runbook before using it as an AI/developer</li></ol><p>instruction.</p><ol><li>Add one source/authority/queue/identity/auth/history matrix to the existing</li></ol><p>architecture and playback pages.</p><ol><li>Make integrations.md and api-endpoint-catalog.md current indexes for the</li></ol><p>newer Qobuz, UPnP, mobile, iOS, and external-hardware surfaces.</p><ol><li>Keep current and target iOS architecture explicitly separated.</li><li>Preserve the canonical docs/wiki-source/ hierarchy and use focused pages</li></ol><p>only where an existing hub cannot carry a contract safely.</p><ol><li>When using a future DeepWiki review, record its revision and compare it to</li></ol><p>HEAD before accepting any architectural claim.</p><h2 id="11-remaining-uncertainties">11. Remaining uncertainties</h2><p>This audit intentionally stopped at source/documentation comparison. The following remain outside its evidence:</p><ul><li>live behavior of every external renderer and hardware integration</li><li>current service state on the deployed Pi5</li><li>exact systemd/PM2 unit behavior where DeepWiki did not include the files</li><li>whether every current deployment host has the same configuration</li><li>provider-side Qobuz behavior outside the PiBuZ/Server contracts</li><li>native iOS implementation details beyond the Server-facing contract</li></ul><p>Those questions require separate, explicitly authorized runtime or repository audits. They do not weaken the main conclusion: DeepWiki accurately captures the older Sonuvi foundation, but current architectural continuity depends on the source-backed boundaries documented above.</p><h2 id="12-code-first-repository-documentation-accuracy-pass">12. Code-first repository documentation accuracy pass</h2><p>The reconciliation follow-up was performed against current main at <code>673e5037731443db17b82df6b293733fb030efa9</code> and the implementation currently present in <code>src/</code>, <code>moode-nowplaying-api.mjs</code>, <code>scripts/</code>, and the retained operational documents. The comparison order was source code first, then canonical <code>docs/wiki-source/</code>, then root documentation and runbooks, with DeepWiki treated as derived evidence. This pass did not change application code, API behavior, configuration, deployment, or the iOS repository.</p><h3 id="classification-ledger">Classification ledger</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Code-first result</th><th>Repository documentation classification</th><th>DeepWiki relationship</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Playback authority</td><td>MPD owns Home/local/radio MPD playback; PiBuZ owns active Qobuz Connect state; Sonuvi owns the UPnP logical queue/session; native devices report through current Server contracts</td><td>Canonical architecture/playback pages now agree. Root <code>ARCHITECTURE.md</code> was incomplete because it implied a universal MPD authority; it now scopes MPD to its domain</td><td>DeepWiki is outdated/incomplete when its MPD-centered description is read as the whole system</td></tr><tr><td>Qobuz Connect and handoff</td><td><code>pibuz-qobuz-control.mjs</code> guards play/pause/next/previous/seek/queue-jump with current-track/queue evidence and read-after-write verification; release requires confirmed inactive ownership</td><td>Runbook 28 and mobile/API pages now distinguish read-only snapshot from guarded control and explicit release. The earlier runbook wording was outdated</td><td>DeepWiki independently predates the control/release lifecycle and repeats the older read-only boundary</td></tr><tr><td>UPnP queue and renderer</td><td><code>mobile-upnp.routes.mjs</code>, <code>upnp-playback-session.mjs</code>, and <code>upnp-playback-queue.mjs</code> implement bearer-safe routes, revisions, session generations, explicit takeover, and renderer transport</td><td>Canonical UPnP/API pages now agree. The UPnP page&#x27;s implemented AVTransport path was incorrectly labeled future and is corrected; root architecture was incomplete</td><td>DeepWiki page 7.9 is useful but revision-stale on readiness and current control details</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile API and Server/iOS boundary</td><td>Mobile sessions are signed scoped bearers; current routes cover now-playing, queue, Audio Info, Qobuz, UPnP, local-source, playback events, and recent history; Track Key remains server/web-only</td><td>Canonical mobile/API pages and the new Server→iOS handoff agree. Root docs were incomplete about the mobile credential/contract boundary and are corrected</td><td>DeepWiki is incomplete relative to the current bearer route family and target/current iOS split</td></tr><tr><td>History and Last.fm</td><td>MPD polling excludes stream/AirPlay/podcast/Alexa paths; native event routes accept supported catalog/radio/podcast observations; Server owns threshold, deduplication, local history, and Last.fm submission; Qobuz ownership suppresses MPD attribution</td><td>Canonical history page agreed; retained compatibility guide was incomplete/outdated about the exact formula and native non-MPD events and is corrected</td><td>DeepWiki page 6.6 is independently mislabeled and does not document the current history pipeline</td></tr><tr><td>Audio diagnostics</td><td>Track-Key <code>/config/moode/audio-info</code> gathers moOde rows and optional ALSA/source diagnostics; bearer <code>/v1/mobile/audio-info</code> sanitizes rows and <code>audio-info.v1</code> provenance</td><td>Canonical diagnostics/API pages agree; retained diagnostics guide was incomplete about the separate mobile boundary and is corrected</td><td>DeepWiki page 9.7 has a sound foundation but is incomplete/stale on the mobile wrapper and measured-vs-configured distinction</td></tr><tr><td>Deployment and recovery</td><td>The repository helper and ops docs define the Pi5 target, path-sensitive restart boundary, and post-deploy verification; live runtime state was not asserted</td><td>Canonical deployment/ops docs agree; no live-service claim was added from source inspection alone</td><td>DeepWiki is operationally incomplete; its installer view is not evidence of live deployment state</td></tr><tr><td>Historical documentation layers</td><td><code>docs/wiki-source/sources/</code> is explicitly tooling support; compatibility guides and runbooks are retained secondary references; runbook 28/29 now label historical phases</td><td>Current-vs-historical boundaries are now explicit in the affected pages rather than deleting useful history</td><td>DeepWiki remains a derived historical snapshot, not a second authoring hierarchy</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The requested classification labels resolve as follows:</p><ul><li><strong>Code and documentation agree:</strong> canonical playback-authority, API,</li></ul><p>diagnostics, deployment, and history pages now match the inspected source; live service state remains a separate question.</p><ul><li><strong>Documentation is outdated:</strong> the retained history guide, UPnP future-path</li></ul><p>wording, and older Qobuz runbook control description were corrected.</p><ul><li><strong>Documentation is incomplete:</strong> root architecture/config and the retained</li></ul><p>diagnostics guide omitted current authority or mobile-contract boundaries; those omissions were corrected.</p><ul><li><strong>Documentation contradicts another document:</strong> the historical read-only</li></ul><p>wording in Runbook 28 conflicted with current control code and the current canonical API pages; the runbook now labels the historical layer and current control surface separately.</p><ul><li><strong>DeepWiki is outdated despite accurate repository documentation:</strong> its</li></ul><p>Qobuz read-only boundary and current UPnP readiness/control omissions are revision-stale while the source-backed repository pages describe the newer implementation.</p><ul><li><strong>Implementation behavior is ambiguous or insufficiently verified:</strong> live</li></ul><p>Pi5 service state, external renderer media-response behavior, provider-side Qobuz account behavior, and the future iOS catalog/synchronization contract were not inferred from source or DeepWiki.</p><h3 id="repository-documentation-errors-versus-independent-deepwiki-inaccuracies">Repository documentation errors versus independent DeepWiki inaccuracies</h3><p>The following were <strong>repository documentation defects corrected in this reconciliation</strong>: the root architecture&#x27;s universal-sounding MPD authority and omission of Qobuz/UPnP/mobile boundaries; the retained history guide&#x27;s imprecise threshold and blanket exclusion wording; the UPnP page&#x27;s future label for implemented AVTransport/session behavior; the mobile diagnostics omission in the retained diagnostics guide; and the Qobuz runbook&#x27;s ambiguous description of the snapshot adapter as the complete control surface.</p><p>The following are <strong>independent DeepWiki inaccuracies or revision limits</strong>: the indexed revision predates the current Qobuz control/release and expanded mobile/UPnP contracts; page 6.6 is mislabeled for history/scrobbling while its body discusses About/Apple metadata; and page 7.9 describes the older read-only Qobuz boundary and lacks current readiness/control details. DeepWiki also cannot establish live service state, external renderer behavior, or the approved future iOS catalog contracts from its page text.</p><h3 id="current-versus-planned-architecture">Current versus planned architecture</h3><p>The current Server-backed opaque <code>MobileTrack</code> and mobile queue/history contracts remain the implementation boundary. The approved iOS-device-owned canonical Catalog, provider aggregation, identity merging, metadata-conflict rules, and server-independent playback remain planned and intentionally unresolved. The retained history and compatibility material is useful only when read with its current/legacy labels; it is not a substitute for source verification.</p><p><em>Code-first pass reviewed: 2026-10-20 America/Chicago.</em></p></article><script>(function(){var p=(location.pathname.split("/").pop()||"README.html");document.querySelectorAll("nav a[href]").forEach(function(a){if(a.getAttribute("href")===p){a.classList.add("nav-current");var d=a.closest("details");if(d)d.open=true;}});})();</script><script>(function(){var i=document.getElementById("nav-search");if(!i)return;})();</script></body></html>
