 <!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>mobile-now-playing</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=20260922"><script src="search-index.js?v=20260922"></script></head><body><nav><h1><a href="README.html">Sonuvi documentation</a></h1><div class="meta">Canonical source: <code>docs/wiki-source/</code></div><details><summary><strong>Start</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="README.html">README</a></li><li><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a></li><li><a href="using-now-playing.html">Using Sonuvi</a></li><li><a href="core-concepts.html">Core Concepts</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Displays</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="displays.html">Displays</a></li><li><a href="user-interfaces.html">User Interfaces</a></li><li><a href="kiosk-interface.html">Kiosk</a></li><li><a href="visualizer-in-embedded-mode.html">Visualizer</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Playback and Library</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="playback-features.html">Playback Features</a></li><li><a href="queue-and-playback-model.html">Queue and Playback</a></li><li><a href="queue-wizard-internals.html">Queue Wizard</a></li><li><a href="media-library.html">Media Library</a></li><li><a href="listen-on-device.html">Listen on Device</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Integrations</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="integrations.html">Integrations</a></li><li><a href="alexa-interface.html">Alexa</a></li><li><a href="youtube-interface.html">YouTube</a></li><li><a href="radio-interface.html">Radio</a></li><li><a href="mabel-integration.html">Mabel</a></li><li><a href="jukebox-priority-model.html">Jukebox Priority</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Administration</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="configuration-and-administration.html">Configuration and Administration</a></li><li><a href="config-interface.html">Config</a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">Diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">Deployment and Ops</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Developer Reference</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="developer-reference.html">Developer Reference</a></li><li><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a></li><li><a href="api-service-overview.html">API Overview</a></li><li><a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">API Catalog</a></li><li><a href="source-map.html">Source Map</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Troubleshooting and Maintenance</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="troubleshooting-and-technical-notes.html">Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="playback-issue-triage-runbook.html">Playback Triage</a></li><li><a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html">Display Triage</a></li><li><a href="documentation-sources-audit.html">Documentation Audit</a></li><li><a href="wiki-operations.html">Wiki Operations</a></li></ul></details></nav><article><h1 id="mobile-home-moode-now-playing">Mobile Home moOde Now Playing</h1><p>This page defines the bearer-authenticated current-state contract used by the native iPhone/iPad client. It keeps the controller-tablet <code>/now-playing</code> truth surface authoritative without exposing its Track-Key/admin boundary to the mobile app.</p><h2 id="endpoint">Endpoint</h2><pre><code>GET /v1/mobile/now-playing
-Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The route requires the existing <code>mobile-api</code> bearer scope. A Track Key alone must receive HTTP 401. The native client never calls <code>/now-playing</code> directly.</p><h2 id="response">Response</h2><pre><code>{
+Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The route requires the existing <code>mobile-api</code> bearer scope. A Track Key alone must receive HTTP 401. The native client never calls <code>/now-playing</code> directly.</p><p>This is a Server-backed current-state contract. It does not make the current Server catalog permanent: the approved native target is an iOS-device-owned canonical catalog with provider observations and server-independent native playback, but identity merging, enrichment conflict rules, and synchronization contracts for that target are not implemented here. Until those contracts are approved, the client must treat the Server&#x27;s opaque <code>MobileTrack</code> identity and the routes in this page as authoritative for Home playback, metadata, artwork, and history handoff.</p><h2 id="response">Response</h2><pre><code>{
   &quot;ok&quot;: true,
   &quot;available&quot;: true,
   &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Example Track&quot;,
@@ -56,9 +56,28 @@ Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The server inv
 Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;
 
 GET /v1/mobile/audio-info
-Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p><code>/v1/mobile/next-up</code> returns the web controller&#x27;s target-aware successor. The iPad presents it as <strong>Next Playing</strong> and opens the shared Live Queue when tapped. The shelf also shows the current queue position/length from the now-playing payload or the durable device queue.</p><p>When Live Queue is selected as a Home discovery row, the native remote poll also reads the complete upcoming queue and reconciles that row. This covers queue additions made by another controller; local playback uses the device queue directly.</p><p><code>/v1/mobile/audio-info</code> invokes the existing Track-Key-protected moOde reader server-side and returns only sanitized <code>section</code>, <code>key</code>, and <code>value</code> rows plus an optional fetch timestamp. It never exposes the moOde source URL, Track Key, MPD file path, or raw admin response to the native client.</p><h2 id="local-audio-sourcecache">Local audio source/cache</h2><p>The server catalog and queue remain authoritative when the native client plays to This iPhone/iPad. The attached SSD and Application Support store are byte sources below the normal canonical <code>MobileTrack</code> flow; they are not additional catalogs, queues, playlists, or track identities.</p><p>The client obtains an authenticated availability manifest:</p><pre><code>GET /v1/mobile/local-source/manifest
+Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p><code>/v1/mobile/next-up</code> returns the web controller&#x27;s target-aware successor. The iPad presents it as <strong>Next Playing</strong> and opens the shared Live Queue when tapped. The shelf also shows the current queue position/length from the now-playing payload or the durable device queue.</p><p>When Live Queue is selected as a Home discovery row, the native remote poll also reads the complete upcoming queue and reconciles that row. This covers queue additions made by another controller; local playback uses the device queue directly.</p><p><code>/v1/mobile/audio-info</code> invokes the existing Track-Key-protected moOde reader server-side and returns sanitized <code>section</code>, <code>key</code>, and <code>value</code> rows plus an optional fetch timestamp. Source/file-path rows are reduced to a source class such as <code>Local file</code> or <code>Network stream</code>; the response never exposes the moOde source URL, Track Key, MPD file path, raw admin response, or moOde PHP session identifier to the native client.</p><p>When this route is opened, the Server requests the optional on-demand diagnostics view from the Track-Key route. The response may include the backward-compatible, versioned <code>diagnostics</code> object:</p><pre><code>{
+  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;audio-info.v1&quot;,
+  &quot;capturedAt&quot;: &quot;2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z&quot;,
+  &quot;freshness&quot;: {
+    &quot;mode&quot;: &quot;on-demand&quot;,
+    &quot;capturedAt&quot;: &quot;2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z&quot;,
+    &quot;hardwareMeasuredAt&quot;: &quot;2026-10-15T18:00:00.000Z&quot;
+  },
+  &quot;renderer&quot;: &quot;mpd&quot;,
+  &quot;sourceFormat&quot;: { &quot;format&quot;: &quot;FLAC 24 bit 96 kHz, Stereo&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 24, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2 },
+  &quot;decodedPcm&quot;: { &quot;format&quot;: &quot;PCM 24 bit 96 kHz, Stereo&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 24, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2 },
+  &quot;sourceFile&quot;: { &quot;container&quot;: &quot;FLAC&quot;, &quot;codec&quot;: &quot;FLAC&quot;, &quot;codecStatus&quot;: &quot;verified&quot;, &quot;codecKind&quot;: &quot;lossless&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 24, &quot;bitDepthStatus&quot;: &quot;verified&quot;, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2, &quot;encodedBitrateBps&quot;: 4200000, &quot;encodedBitrateStatus&quot;: &quot;reported&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;source-file&quot; },
+  &quot;decodedAudio&quot;: { &quot;format&quot;: &quot;PCM&quot;, &quot;codec&quot;: &quot;PCM&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 24, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2, &quot;pcmBitrateBps&quot;: 4608000, &quot;pcmBitrateStatus&quot;: &quot;calculated&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;decoded-reported&quot; },
+  &quot;configuredOutput&quot;: { &quot;alsaMode&quot;: &quot;plughw&quot;, &quot;audioChain&quot;: &quot;MPD → plughw → Device&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;configured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: false },
+  &quot;hardwareOutput&quot;: { &quot;format&quot;: &quot;S32_LE&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 32, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;hardware-measured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: true },
+  &quot;output&quot;: { &quot;format&quot;: &quot;S32_LE&quot;, &quot;bitDepth&quot;: 32, &quot;sampleRateHz&quot;: 96000, &quot;channels&quot;: 2, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;hardware-measured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: true },
+  &quot;processing&quot;: { &quot;resampling&quot;: &quot;Off&quot;, &quot;replayGain&quot;: &quot;off&quot;, &quot;normalization&quot;: &quot;off&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;configured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: false },
+  &quot;volume&quot;: { &quot;type&quot;: &quot;Fixed (0dB output)&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;configured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: false },
+  &quot;conversion&quot;: { &quot;status&quot;: &quot;unknown&quot;, &quot;valueType&quot;: &quot;not-measured&quot;, &quot;measured&quot;: false }
+}</code></pre><p><code>sourceFormat</code> and <code>decodedPcm</code> are moOde/renderer-reported values. The additive <code>sourceFile</code> object is the authoritative normalized source view: lossless PCM-based files may expose verified encoded bit depth, while AAC, MP3, Opus, Vorbis, and other perceptual codecs expose encoded bitrate but report source bit depth as <code>not-applicable</code>. <code>sourceFile.codecStatus</code> is <code>verified</code> when the bounded local-file probe identified the codec, <code>reported</code> when provider metadata supplied it, and <code>unavailable</code> otherwise. <code>decodedAudio</code> describes decoder PCM precision and a calculated nominal PCM throughput; it does not reuse the encoded bitrate shown by moOde. <code>output</code> is the measured ALSA endpoint view. The <code>configuredOutput</code>, <code>processing</code>, and <code>volume</code> sections describe configured state and are never presented as hardware measurements. <code>hardwareOutput</code> is the bounded, read-only ALSA <code>/proc/asound</code> observation; it is absent or marked unavailable when no playback stream exposes parameters. <code>conversion</code> remains unknown because ALSA <code>hw_params</code> cannot prove every transformation before the hardware endpoint.</p><p>When diagnostics are requested, the legacy mobile <code>Decoded to</code> row is also corrected for verified lossy sources so an encoded bitrate is not displayed as decoded PCM throughput. The ordinary non-diagnostics legacy response is unchanged for compatibility.</p><h2 id="local-audio-sourcecache">Local audio source/cache</h2><p>The server catalog and queue remain authoritative when the native client plays to This iPhone/iPad. The attached SSD and Application Support store are byte sources below the normal canonical <code>MobileTrack</code> flow; they are not additional catalogs, queues, playlists, or track identities.</p><p>The client obtains an authenticated availability manifest:</p><pre><code>GET /v1/mobile/local-source/manifest
 Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The response maps canonical track IDs to library-relative paths and integrity evidence. The client validates the attached file and otherwise uses the normal media authorization endpoint. SSD disconnect, absent files, stale size entries, and reconnect are cache misses/recovery, not library or playback mode changes.</p><p>Native device playback reports progress through the same bearer session:</p><pre><code>POST /v1/mobile/playback/events
 Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;
 Content-Type: application/json
 
-{&quot;trackId&quot;:&quot;trk_...&quot;,&quot;sessionId&quot;:&quot;device-session&quot;,&quot;state&quot;:&quot;progress&quot;,&quot;elapsedSec&quot;:78,&quot;durationSec&quot;:214}</code></pre><p>The server resolves the track ID and feeds the shared listening-history qualification/idempotency path. The client never submits a filesystem path, synthetic SSD ID, or alternate queue identity.</p><p>Native podcast playback is the feature-specific exception to the catalog ID shape: the client uses an opaque <code>podcast-...</code> episode identity for its local device queue, and the bearer route resolves that identity to the downloaded episode&#x27;s server-owned MPD path and metadata before recording history or invoking the native APNs bridge. This keeps podcast paths out of the client while allowing podcast starts to receive the same track-change notification behavior as music.</p><p><em>Last reviewed: 2026-10-02 16:55 America/Chicago</em></p></article><script>(function(){var p=(location.pathname.split("/").pop()||"README.html");document.querySelectorAll("nav a[href]").forEach(function(a){if(a.getAttribute("href")===p){a.classList.add("nav-current");var d=a.closest("details");if(d)d.open=true;}});})();</script><script>(function(){var i=document.getElementById("nav-search");if(!i)return;})();</script></body></html>
